cause callers that use `batch=True` would be expecting json output but the non-batched variant doesn't return it.  At this point, though, it seems like all annexrepo methods return json for both batched and non-batched, so this shouldn't be an issue.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1526994376,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MDk4MjYwOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-390982608"},"message":";-) Thanks for the translation!","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527012147,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTA4NTU0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391085542"},"message":"It seems to me that we should have a switch that turns on/off batched processing, and it should default to off on windows.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527013638,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTA5MzU3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391093570"},"message":"I thought to suggest the same.  I am afraid though that many operations will literally \"crawl\" (and not `datalad crawl`) with a per-file invocation of git-annex.  May be it would be worth exploring the initial problem (original description is \"too concise\" IMHO to deduce anything) and see if it could be addressed without removing the use of batched processes?  I think that git-annex itself uses batched versions of some git commands on windows as well, and I guess it works ok, isn't it @joeyh?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527015031,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTEwMTA1MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391101051"},"message":"Few thoughts:\n\n- we ar