thub-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTExMjI5MQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391112291"},"message":"I wonder if at least some of those aren't real issues of us (or GitPython) not closing some files before trying to annihilate them/directories.  E.g. on linux this one works \"just fine\" (too many python opens since was playing around, file could be generated outside):\n\n```shell\n$\u003e rm -rf /tmp/test; mkdir /tmp/test; python -c 'f=open(\"/tmp/test/1\", \"w\"); f.write(\"1\"); f.close(); f2=open(\"/tmp/test/1\"); import shutil; shutil.rmtree(\"/tmp/test/\"); print(\"READ: %s\" % f2.read())' \nREAD: 1\n```\nand I guess should fail on Windows?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527017581,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTExMzYwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391113607"},"message":"Probably, Q is just how would change the code? Not remove?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527018897,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTExOTc1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391119754"},"message":"I can only reply with another Q: who would change/remove what code?\n\nIf I cared about Windows, I would have tried to check if it is possible to see which files are still open in that directory before trying to remove it -- and if there are some, then deduce what module/process might still keep them open... actually it could probably be done even first within our code on Linux where we do have utilities such as `lsof` to see that  eg at `c:\\projects\\datalad\\datalad\\utils.py\", line 325, in rmtemp` point","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527019156,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTEyMDk3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391120975"},"message":"Which seems to bring us back full circle. Have a switch to turn it off and see whether the underlying functionality is working or can be made to work at all. And if, try to make it faster....if.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1527092437,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQwODk5Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391408993"},"message":"Michael Hanke wrote:\n\u003e [00:12:49] PermissionError: [WinError 32] The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process: 'C:\\\\Users\\\\appveyor\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\1\\\\tmp-page2annexjkinu2k6'\n\nIf it helps, Windows has this fun behavior where opening a file for\nread implicitly locks it, preventing a concurrent write.\n\n(Bear in mind that Windows virus scanners may open any file for read at\nany time..)\n\nNaturally, this caused all manner of fun in git-annex on windows.\n\nThe general approach used in Windows to get around this seems to be to\nbusy-wait when a write fails, in hopes that the readers will get out of\nthe way. I kid you not. Busy-waiting is built into Windows api's \nsuch as createFile. There are also some less-used read modes that don't\nlock the file.\n\nThis also causes problems with recursive directory removal, since if \nanything has a file in the directory open for read, removing it may fail\nand then deleting the directory fail.\n\nEnjoy your Windows Experience (TM)!\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1527092941,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQxMjMyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391412325"},"message":"Have you guys considered using WSL (aka \"bash for windows\") instead of\ntrying to support native Windows? I would kind of prefer to go that\ndirection with git-annex.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1527093269,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQxNDU2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391414563"},"message":"@joeyh Yes, that is a parallel effort: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2475","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527104223,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTY0MjY1MzgzOQ=="},"title":"Disable batched annex on windows? (also on inability to rmtree etc due to locked files)","was":"Disable batched annex on windows? (also on inability to rmtree etc due to locked files)"},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1527104311,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM5MTQ3MTE2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-391471165"},"message":"(possibly) relevant issues within GitPython (of which there are many): https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/issues?utf8=%E2%9C%93\u0026q=label%3Atag.leaks+ , just now detected the one for cat-file --batched with #2542 helper","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1536170633,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQxODgyNTQ5OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2518#issuecomment-418825498"},"message":"In this particular case (not that things would work right away, but it is a step forward), I think it was our genuine mistake: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/2791/commits/369d21fc5b37dd05e8bae478b82005d3ca9dfe6a","files":null}]}